<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan's Acer Sertek up on debut.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's Acer Sertek up on debut.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newcomer Acer Sertek Co, a unit of Taiwan computer giant Acer Inc, soared by the daily seven percent limit in early trade on Wednesday, its first day of listing on the Taiwan Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>After 50 minutes, the firm was limit up, surging T$2.4 to T$37.4.</p>
<p>&quot;It's normal celebration-buying for a new listed company,&quot; said Chen Han-chung of Yungli Securities.</p>
<p>&quot;Recent good performance by the electronics sector should make Acer Sertek's honeymoon even longer,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>Acer Sertek, a computer manufacturer, is 48 percent owned by Acer Inc.</p>
<p>Its main business includes computer hardware, software and semiconductor components. Most of its products supply Taiwan's domestic market.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
